# SFZ edition of songs/epic/a_comma_higher.sm. Original score and renders preserved.
# Instrumentation and faders revised; written notes, tuning, form, timing and binaural settings retained.
# Listening candidate: automated measurements are not a human listening verdict.
# A Comma Higher. A through-composed progressive-metal / modal-jazz / golden-modal epic in 36-ET, 9:48.
# One idea carries it: the song starts on C and ends on ^C, one sixth-step (33 cents, the 36-ET golden comma)
# higher, after "the comma pump" of textbook Chapter 34 lifts the whole tonality one note at a time.
# Listen for: the golden pedal intro bending into a C major power chord; a 7/8 Phrygian-dominant riff; a verse
# and chorus whose tune (the "phi" theme) returns as a modal-jazz solo, a ballad and a coda; a modal jazz head
# that moves from C dorian to C golden7 (the golden Dorian) and up a comma, like So What's half-step lift; the
# seven golden7 modes, brightest to darkest, traded between horn and guitar; the golden jazz cadence home to
# Cmaj7; golden giant steps; a 7/8 decatonic riff built from the two golden pentatonics; golden planing (a C
# major line in three keys at once); a 13/16 bridge; a guitar solo round the golden circle; a ballad on the
# golden Neapolitan; then thirteen golden chords climbing to ^Cg, and the riff and chorus a comma higher.
#
# Golden techniques and where they are (textbook chapters):
#   veil, coda      golden pedal: over a held C only Cg, ^Abg and vFg can sound (ch37); the coda does it on ^C
#   door            the golden projection reversed, Cg -> C: C golden7 opens onto C, the dominant of F
#                   harmonic minor, the Western key nearest C golden7 (ch35)
#   chorus_2        golden deceptive cadence Eb - vEg - Eg - Fm (ch29); golden mediant Ab - Cg - C into the riff
#   head_*          modal key changes: C dorian (12-ET) -> C golden7 (3|3 is the golden Dorian, ch36) -> a
#                   comma lift to ^C golden7, "a pure change of plane" (ch34) -> back to C dorian
#   mode_60..06     the seven modes of golden7 on C, brightest to darkest, one note lower each time by 5
#                   sixth-steps (ch36); the two darkest have no golden tonic (Cdim(^^3,v5), Csus2(vvvv5))
#   cadence         golden jazz cadence Dg7 - vGg/D - G7 - Baug(v3)/G - ^Ebg(^5)/G - Cmaj7 (ch29); Dg7 is a
#                   chord of the darkest mode, so it is the pivot out of it
#   giant           golden giant steps C - Cg - Ab - Abg - E - Eg - C, the horn on the common tones (ch37)
#   deca_*, axe_solo  the "35" golden decatonic (golden10_36, ch36): a riff alternating its two golden
#                   pentatonics, the golden circle walk Cg - ^Abg - vFg - C#g - ^Ag - vF#g - Dg and back
#   planing         golden planing = three-key polytonality: a C major line with vE major and ^G major above it (ch37)
#   deca_13         13/16 over vEg -> Cg (leading-tone resolution) and C#g -> Cg (the golden Neapolitan, ch37)
#   still           golden home on golden timbres: the phi theme in C golden7, Bg -> Cg (every voice up a semitone)
#   pump_a..d       the comma pump: Cg - ^Abg - vFg - C#g - ^Ag - vF#g - Dg - ^Bbg - vGg - Ebg - ^Bg - vAbg - Eg - ^Cg,
#                   each chord keeping two notes and raising one a semitone (ch34); the lead sings the top voice,
#                   ^G ^Ab ^A ^Bb ^B ^C, and lands on the new tonic
#   summit_*        riff, verse, pre-chorus and chorus a comma higher (^C phrygian dominant, ^F harmonic minor,
#                   ^Ab major); the last chorus has the golden deceptive cadence ^Eb - Eg - ^Eg - ^Fm
#   coda            golden Picardy ^Cm - ^Cm(^3) - ^Cg - ^C (ch29)
#
# Engine extensions used: per-section meters (meter=7/8, "5/4 3+2", "13/16 3+3+3+2+2"), the named golden modes
# (key="C golden7_51", golden10_36) and the phrygian_dominant mode. The distorted guitar is a patch instrument
# that distorts each note on its own, so golden chords keep their shape through the distortion.
song "A Comma Higher" 138 4/4 C fps=30 seed=1301 tail=6 tuning=36edo
patch axe str=string(t60=1.6, brightness=.93, pick=.003) sh=shaper(drive=.8) cab=filter(mode=lp, cutoff=4200, q=1.2, keytrack=0) env=env(a=.002, d=.4, s=.85, r=.07) amp=vca out=out(level=.6)
patch axe str>sh sh>cab cab>amp env>amp.gain amp>out vel>sh.drive*.3
inst axe=patch/axe bass=bass/v0(cutoff=850, drive=2.2, env_amt=1.6, env_decay=.12, sub=.4, glide=.03) lead(voices=3, detune=2, vib_depth=6, vib_delay=.35, cutoff=3800, release=.2) horn=clean/organ(partials=7, rolloff=1.5, even=.6, attack=.035, release=.18, vel_bright=.8) epiano=sampler/fm_piano keys=sampler/grand_piano organ=clean/organ(partials=9, rolloff=1.25, attack=.02, release=.25) gold=clean/golden_pad(release=2) bell=clean/glass gtr=string_pluck/still(brightness=.8, t60=2.4) low=clean/bass
kit kick=kick/v0(tune=55, sweep=26, decay=.28, click=.65, click_tone=4500, drive=2) snare=snare/v0(tone=205, tone_mix=.5, snap=.65, noise_decay=.2, drive=1.5) hat=hat/v0(decay=.045) ride=hat/v0(decay=.3, hp=3500, color=6500, metal=.85, tune=.8) cym=hat/v0_open(decay=1.4, hp=3200, metal=.75) tom1=kick/v0(tune=150, sweep=7, sweep_time=.05, decay=.35, click=.15, drive=1.2) tom2=kick/v0(tune=105, sweep=7, sweep_time=.05, decay=.42, click=.15, drive=1.2) tom3=kick/v0(tune=78, sweep=8, sweep_time=.05, decay=.5, click=.15, drive=1.2)

# --- harmony -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
prog veil_p    "Cg:2 ^Abg:1 vFg:1 Cg:2 ^Abg:1 ^Abg7:1 Cg:1 vFg:1 ^Abg:1 Cg:1"
prog door_p    "Cg:1 C:1"
prog verse_p   "Fm:1 Db:1 C:1 Fm:1 Fm:1 Db:1 Bbm:1 C:1"
prog pre_p     "Db:1 Eb:1 Fm:1 Eb:1"
prog chorus_p  "Ab:1 Fm:1 Db:1 Eb:1 Db:1 Eb:1 Fm:1 Ab:1"
prog chorus2_p "Ab:1 Fm:1 Db:1 Eb:1 Db:1 Eb:0.5 vEg:0.25 Eg:0.25 Fm:1 Ab:0.75 Cg:0.25"
prog dorian_p  "Cm7:2 F7:2 Cm7:2 F7:1 Cm7:1"
prog goldor_p  "Cg7:2 vFg7:2 Cg7:2 vFg7:1 Cg7:1"
